            <ArticleTitle>Improved pituitary function after V-P shunt insertion in pseudotumor cerebri.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>303-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pseudotumor Cerebri is a disease of cerebrospinal fluid pressure regulation. This disease has also been associated with endocrine disorders like Cushing's syndrome, hypoparathyroidism, hypothyroidism, hyperthyroidism and Addison's disease. In this paper we report a 30-year-old male patient with hypoparathyroidism presenting with pseudotumor cerebri and diminished anterior pituitary function that improved after a ventricular-peritoneal (VP) shunt insertion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
